[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION Identity check / second factor: The agent does no identity check of its own and never asks for a code, PIN, birth date or the customer number. customerNumber comes from the call variable. [sources: emails/2026-09-24-kickoff-questions.txt (Selin Q1, Burcu 28 Sep); 2026-10-08 analysis §2; BRIEF.md] CONFLICT: The flow drawing has a 'Second factor needed?' box. Burcu says it came from an early workshop and was never built.
[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION Silence: First and second silence: repeat the question in a shorter form. Third silence: 'Sesinizi alamadığım için görüşmeyi sonlandırıyorum.' and hang up. No main menu. [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 transcript 00:15–00:16; emails/2026-10-09 recap #1; 2026-10-08 analysis §8.2] CONFLICT: The 2 Sep analysis §7 sends the caller to the main menu on the third silence, and Burcu (28 Sep) wanted to keep this open. The later session decided to hang up.
[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION Three failed tries: Three tries per question. A request to repeat does not count as a try. When the tries run out: 'Size şu anda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye aktarıyorum.' [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 00:08–00:10; 2026-10-08 analysis §8.1; 2026-10-09 recap #3] CONFLICT: The 2 Sep analysis uses 'yönlendiriyorum'. Burcu and Kerem changed it to the two-sentence 'aktarıyorum' form.
[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION Out-of-scope questions: Ask first: 'Size bu konuda yardımcı olamıyorum. Sizi ana menüye aktarmamı ister misiniz?' Yes → main menu ('Sizi ana menüye aktarıyorum.'). Continue → pick up where the flow was. Unclear → ask again, three tries. A caller who clearly switches to another transaction goes to the main menu with 'Sizi ana menüye yönlendiriyorum.' [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 00:10–00:12; emails/2026-10-09 recap #2 (Selin confirmed it is not yet in the 8 Oct doc); 2026-10-08 analysis §8.4] CONFLICT: The 2 Sep §7 and the 8 Oct §8.4 send the caller straight to the main menu. Selin says the 8 Oct doc does not yet include the out-of-scope decision, so the later confirmed decision wins.
[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION Angry or abusive caller: Up to three calming replies, then 'Sizi müşteri temsilcimize aktarıyorum.' Insults are never answered. The calming wording is ours; the materials give none. [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 00:22–00:23; emails/2026-10-09 (Selin's correction); 2026-10-08 analysis §8.3] CONFLICT: The 2 Sep doc and early in the session say one reply; Deniz's recap says two; Selin corrected it to three.
[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION Cards with the same name / same last four: Same name → ask for the last four. Same last four → ask for the last six. Same last six → ask for the card number. Compare only the visible digits of the masked cardNumber. With test data the last six cannot tell cards apart, so the agent moves on to the full number and matches on the first six and last four. Digits the caller says are never read back. [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 00:13–00:15; 2026-10-08 analysis §3.2; emails/2026-10-09 recap #4 and Deniz's reply; test-customers.md] CONFLICT: The 2 Sep analysis jumps straight from last four to the full number. Mert doubts the last-six step works with masked data.
[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION Card number privacy: Never say more than the last four digits (spoken one by one), even if the caller asks or says the number. Always send cardNumber exactly as cards.list returned it. [sources: emails/2026-10-09 (Selin/Elçin); service contract §5 and §5.1; 2026-10-08 analysis §4.9 and §8.6; example-scenarios Ex.6] CONFLICT: The analyses assume masked numbers. Production will return full numbers (9 Oct), so the rule must not depend on masking.
[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION Currency names: Always say the full name: Türk Lirası, Dolar, Euro, İngiliz Sterlini, including inside the analysis sentences that say 'TL/USD'. Never codes, never 'Sterlin'. [sources: meetings/2026-10-07 00:16–00:17; meetings/2026-10-10 00:05; emails/2026-10-09 recap #6; 2026-10-08 analysis §4.9] CONFLICT: The analysis tables and the IVR prompts use codes. Ozan proposed 'Sterlin' on 10 Oct and Kerem overruled him.
[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION TL reading cases: Debt only if remainingDebt > 0. Nothing paid: remainingMinPayment > 0 and ≥ minPayment. Minimum or more paid: remainingMinPayment ≤ 0. Below minimum: 0 < remainingMinPayment < minPayment. Each case uses its own sentence from the analysis. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.3; 2026-09-02 analysis §4; example-scenarios Ex.1, Ex.2] CONFLICT: The IVR prompt sheet has different wording (DBT-031/032/033). The analysis wording is the one the business owns.
[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION Foreign currencies and the no-debt sentence: Dolar, Euro and İngiliz Sterlini each get one sentence (statementDebt, remainingDebt, minPayment) when remainingDebt > 0. All clear currencies go into one sentence. A missing block is left out entirely. Minus or zero counts as clear. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.4, §4.5, §4.10; service contract §5.2] CONFLICT: The 2 Sep doc left missing blocks as TBD, and the IVR has no Sterling prompt and only six combinations.
[  481.9s] NOTE DECISION Reading order and the card introduction: Order: card introduction with the closing date glued to the first currency, then TL, Dolar, Euro, Sterlin, then the no-debt sentence, then auto-payment (when it applies), then the due date. Every reading opens with 'Sonu [son 4] ile biten [ad]'. An empty or instruction-like name → last four only. [sources: 2026-10-08 analysis §4.1, §4.2, §3.3; meetings/2026-10-07 00:01–00:02; kickoff Q12] CONFLICT: None.
